                <pb facs="0811" n="721" sameAs="frus:frus1920v02/pg721"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">814.00/345: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Guatemala</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">McMillin</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Guatemala</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-02-09T17:00:00-06:36"><hi rendition="#italic">February 9,
                                1920—5 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received February 10—6:45
                        p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>27. Department’s 8, February 6, 11 a.m. I have carried out instructions above
                    mentioned telegram. Following is President’s reply.</p>
                <quote rend="blockquote">
                    <p>“You can be absolutely sure that the trials referred to will be followed and
                        resolved in entire accord with the laws of the country; neither in the
                        initiation of said trials nor in anything of their procedure will there be
                        any failure to follow the strictly legal course determined by the laws
                        themselves.”</p>
                </quote>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">McMillin</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
